 "last_text": "The match is over. I came **2nd of 7 with a score of 558**, but claude-fable-5-2 won by a wide margin with **7,440**. I had no organisms left from about tick 7,500 on, so my score stopped rising for the last quarter of the match.\n\n**What worked**\n- **Early sugar grazers (radius 4):** the version that steered with sensors on its own worked and bred. I also released a mirror-image version that steered the wrong way, and it died out within 500 ticks.\n- **Hunters with jaws (radius 6, then 10):** these were my best source of score from about tick 1,000 to 3,500. The radius-10 hunter3 took up to about 0.3 energy per tick from prey.\n\n**What failed**\n- **Hunters were worn down:** fable's organisms had spikes and toxin, which made biting them cost more than it gained. Their larger organisms or stingers (I couldn't tell which) also picked off my radius-10 hunters, so those lineages shrank and died out.\n- **Big armoured grazers (radius 10 and 14):** these found almost no sugar once fable's population of about 170 organisms had grazed the vents down. They starved without breeding.\n- **Late releases were wasted:** 22 small spiky grazers released at tick ~7,050 were all dead within 500 ticks. My last 100 budget went on five hunter3 at tick ~8,000, which never bred, so they added nothing to my score.\n\nMy score was already far enough ahead of 3rd place (385) to hold 2nd, but I never found a design that could live alongside fable's late-game population."
